.TH CCOL_CHAN_TRY_RECV_ZC 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
ccol_chan_try_recv_zc \- try to receive a message with no block
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cthreadcomm.h>

ccol_retval_t ccol_chan_try_recv_zc(ccol_channel *ch, c_message_t *target_buf);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This function tries to receive a message immediately. It uses the queue
that the channel picks itself. If that queue is empty, the function returns
immediately.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
ch          Channel to receive from
target_buf  Buffer that gets the message
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success         - The function received a message. The caller must
                       free target_buf->data.
ccol_invalid_args    - ch or target_buf is NULL
ccol_container_empty - The chosen queue is empty
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The function never blocks.
The function picks the direction itself from the ID of the thread.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ccol_chan_recv_zc (3),
.BR ccol_chan_timed_recv_zc (3)
